apple just announced the brand new ipad  air 4 and there's many reasons to buy  one  but there's also a few things that apple  conveniently  left out which you definitely have to be  aware of  before ordering these things will  literally stop  many of you from buying one and make the  ipad air 4  not worth it depending on what you do i  know at least a few of these will  surprise  all of you as they surprise us when we  figure them out  personally i think that many people will  be better off buying  a used or refurbished 2018 ipad pro  for the same amount or possibly even  less money  which i'll leave some links to down in  the description  or possibly spending the extra money and  getting a lot more features with a 2020  ipad pro  in this video i'll tell you not only  what you'll be missing out on  but also what you'll gain with the new  ipad air if you decide to buy it  so that you can make an informed  decision that you won't regret in the  future  on the outside the ipad air 4 looks  almost identical to the 2018  ipad pro it's very slightly thicker but  also lighter  the only visible difference to the  trained eye is that the power button is  larger  and that's because it's using apple's  new touch id that is embedded  into the power button the screen is  slightly smaller at 10.9 inches instead  of 11  and the resolution is dropped by just a  few pixels to match  you won't notice this in the real world  and i feel like the only reason apple  did that  is to separate it from their 11 inch  ipad pro  it's also fully laminated with p3 color  with true tone and the same grey  anti-reflectivity coating  so almost everything is the same but  there are two specific things  that changed which are a deal breaker  for me  but let's stick to the positives before  we get into the negatives  thankfully apple didn't ditch the quad  stereo speakers  which are a massive upgrade for playing  games and  watching movies along with that it also  takes usb  type c it has support for the new magic  keyboard which is overpriced but i still  absolutely love  and it now supports the apple pencil 2  which also means  if you have the first gen pencil you'll  need to buy the new one  the camera on the back looks identical  to the 2018 ipad pro  but for some reason apple didn't include  the quad led flash  which is actually very handy for  scanning documents  the front camera is still 7 megapixels  but it's also missing true depth sensors  so you won't have access to the memoji  animoji  or the portrait lighting features the  other interesting emission  is the five microphones that sounded  great for facetime calls  now there's only two microphones of  course we'll have to see how much of a  difference we have between the speakers  the cameras and the mics  in our hands-on comparison against the  ipad pro so make sure to subscribe so  you don't miss out on that  there's also a few things that it does  better than the ipad pro  but since i started on the downsides  already let's get into  the biggest disappointments first let's  start with the most  obvious one no face id touch id is  fine but face id on the ipad pro is so  convenient from auto unlocking it by  just pressing on the keyboard to logging  into apps and using safari autofill  without ever having to stop what i am  doing is fantastic  and touch id is definitely a step back  the second  is the lack of pro motion which is a  shame  having that 120hz fluid display is one  of the key features that really stands  out on the ipad pros  not only does it make the ipad feel  super smooth and responsive  but it also allows the refresh rate to  drop down to match your content  so if you're watching a movie it runs at  24 frames per second  which looks like the director intended  and it actually saves  battery life at the same time promotion  is also what makes the ipad pro  by far the best tablet to write or draw  on with latency  so low that it's not even noticeable  since the ipad pro reads the pencil's  location  240 times per second the ipad airs  60 hertz screen will have more than  double the latency so basically the same  performance as the ipad pro  from 2016. the other common spec with  the 2016 ipad pro is the display  brightness the 2017 ipad pros and newer  all support 600 nits of brightness  which is 20 brighter than the new air  not only is that really handy in bright  rooms or outdoors but it also enables  hdr video which makes for a really  nice viewing experience with this new  air you'll not only miss  out on the darker more detailed shadows  and having brighter more realistic  highlights  but it will also use more power with the  display refreshing  more than twice as often as it needs to  now comes the really  weird part which i didn't expect and  that is the performance of the a14  bionic processor  we were surprised to see the apple put  the same processor that will come  in the iphone 12 into this mid-spec  tablet which will be  the first ever five nanometer processor  on the market with 11.8 billion  transistors  which is about 40 more than before apple  mentioned that it's 40  faster than the previous cpu and the  graphics ship is 30  faster which is a really good  improvement when we heard the specs we  figured that the new ipad air will have  a few downsides  but having that new processor will make  it a smart buy to future proof it  and it will perform better than the  older pros but actually  that is not the case those performance  improvements were based on the previous  ipad air  so we started to do the math ourselves  and in geekbench 5 cpu tests we should  get a multi-core score of about 4 000  which is respectable obviously beating  out the a12 in the previous air  but looking closer it is still about 15  slower than the ipad pro from two years  ago  onto graphics we should see a metal  score of about 6000  which once again is a good improvement  compared to b4  but it's not only slower than the 2018  ipad pro as you're probably  expecting by now which by the way is  over 50  faster but even the 2017  10 and a half inch ipad pro looks to be  potentially slightly  faster and then of course the 2020 is at  the very top  with that a12z now of course we don't  know which test apple was going off of  in the real world tests could be  different which will do a wide variety  of tests  once we get it in so make sure to ring  that notification bell  so how in the world can a two or even a  three year old  ipad which can be bought for cheaper  than the new air  be performing so well despite their much  older processors well those use x-series  processors which are designed for  tablets  with more graphics and cpu cores for  example the new a14 bionic has a six  core processor which has four high  efficiency cores  and two high performance cores while the  a12x in that 2018 ipad pro  has an a core processor that doubles the  high performance cores the same thing  goes for graphics with the a14 featuring  four core graphics  instead of seven or eight in the newer  ipad pros  so that's how the old ones are actually  still faster  now with that five nanometer design and  less cpu and gpu cores  we should also be seeing better battery  performance but for some reason apple is  still  advertising the same 10 hours of battery  life  i know that lack of the pro motion does  have some effect  but i guess we'll have to do a real  world battery life test when we get it  in  now the new ipad air does have a few  improvements over that 2018 ipad pro  like the new color options which you  won't get and it also has wi-fi six  but overall i would much rather buy a  used or refurbished 2018 ipad pro for a  similar price  and enjoy having hdr a brighter display  having a flash for documents having  a much smoother experience with the pro  motion display  and using the apple pencil and with that  the very convenient and quick face id  and on top of all of that we have the  much faster cpu  for productivity and gaming now for  those of you who don't want to buy a  used or refurbished ipad  there's also the 2020 ipad pro which  also  has wi-fi six not those colors but it  comes with more improvements  and at about 150 to 200 dollars more  for that extra cash you get all of the  benefits of the 2018 model  but in a brand new device that also gets  more and better cameras  gets lidar has faster cpu and gpu with  potentially double the ram  and double the base storage which is i  think the sweet spot for most people  if 64 gigabytes isn't enough for you on  the air you have to spend 150 dollars  more  to get 256 gigabytes so that's only  about 50  away from a new 128 gigabyte pro  so now that you know the full story it's  going to be up to you to see if the ipad  air  4 is worth it or if all the extras that  come with even the older ipad pros  make those a much better choice let me  know what you think and why  in the comment section i'll go ahead and  leave links to all the models including  the refurb ones down in the video  description  along with links to this sweet ultra  soft premium maxtec  shirt thank you guys for your support  make sure to click that subscribe button  above  as we're going to be doing a ton of  hands-on comparisons as soon as we get  it in  this has been max and i will see you in  the next video
 

